WEBVTT

00:00:02.390 --> 00:00:04.410
Be still!

00:00:02.390 --> 00:00:04.410
Sink!

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:29.550
<b></b>See You Again on Another Quiet Blue Sea

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:41.180
Where am I?

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:46.640
Oh, that's right...

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:48.480
I'm back...

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:49.610
at Sasebo.

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:03.070
Oh, yeah...

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:07.940
I'm back.

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:19.060
<b>See You Again on Another Quiet Blue Sea</b>

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:44.950
<b>Sasebo</b>

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:51.490
Mogami...

00:03:51.490 --> 00:03:54.110
Watch out! No collisions!

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:55.820
Sorry...

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:59.500
So, you're finally awake, Princess?

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:03.380
Still not in top form, huh?

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:06.160
You need to be in bed, Shigure.

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:09.140
I'm fine. Just fine...

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:14.110
See? You need more rest...

00:04:17.450 --> 00:04:21.000
Mogami, you're safe...

00:04:21.950 --> 00:04:23.190
I'm glad.

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:27.090
Of course I am.

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:30.200
This time, I didn't collide with anybody.

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:47.260
What about the others? And Yamashiro?

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:52.890
They're fine.

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:54.470
They made it back to base.

00:04:54.470 --> 00:04:55.870
The mission...

00:04:57.680 --> 00:05:02.680
Operation Shou-Gou was a tactical success.

00:05:03.530 --> 00:05:10.270
Our fleet was in awful shape, but 
we made it back to the Naval District.

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:14.830
It's a miracle, I think.

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:18.040
Oh, I was right.

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:19.700
Then, Yamashiro...

00:05:19.700 --> 00:05:22.090
Where are Yamashiro and Fusou?

00:05:22.780 --> 00:05:26.470
Fusou's at the entrance 
to the Naval District.

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:30.010
I came to get you, just in 
case you were awake.

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:36.970
She's... saying her last
 goodbyes to the admiral.

00:05:36.970 --> 00:05:39.160
Her last... what?

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:42.560
Let's go. I'll help you walk.

00:05:55.140 --> 00:05:56.330
Admiral...

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:10.800
Fusou.

00:06:11.730 --> 00:06:14.770
Don't say a word, Admiral.

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:18.690
I'm very happy.

00:06:22.220 --> 00:06:25.760
After all, Yamashiro and I...

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:28.870
Yes, we both made it out of that strait.

00:06:29.810 --> 00:06:31.660
Right, Yamashiro?

00:06:32.420 --> 00:06:33.680
Yamashiro?

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:36.700
We'll never fight again, though.

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:40.080
Sister, let go of me.

00:06:41.070 --> 00:06:44.270
Of course. Sorry, Yamashiro.

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:50.290
Fusou Class Battleship, Fusou.

00:06:52.410 --> 00:06:54.490
Fusou Class 2, Yamashiro.

00:06:55.880 --> 00:07:00.560
You are both released from 
Reserve Status 4 as of today.

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:02.010
Yes, sir!

00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:07.140
Thank you for everything... for all you did.

00:07:08.310 --> 00:07:09.380
Farewell.

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:16.080
Yamashiro!

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:21.250
Oh, Shigure.

00:07:24.620 --> 00:07:28.090
Finally awake, huh, sleepyhead?

00:07:28.470 --> 00:07:29.470
Yamashiro!

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:32.630
I'm glad you're safe, I guess.

00:07:33.250 --> 00:07:34.470
Yamashiro!

00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:38.990
That's right. We're leaving the fleet.

00:07:39.530 --> 00:07:44.350
We have to. We don't have the strength
 left to fight as Fleet Girls.

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:47.080
Yamashiro...

00:07:48.410 --> 00:07:52.450
Michishio and Destroyer Division 4 
left the fleet before we did.

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:57.570
They can't hold the equipment anymore, 
so there was no other option.

00:07:57.570 --> 00:08:01.910
As of now, 1st Striking Force, 
3rd Section has been disbanded.

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:15.950
We were lucky enough to make it out 
of that strait alive, though.

00:08:16.440 --> 00:08:17.700
Yamashiro.

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:25.450
It's up to you two, now.

00:08:27.100 --> 00:08:30.420
We leave the admiral and
 the fleet in your hands.

00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:37.060
What's wrong? Aren't you "Shigure of Sasebo"?

00:08:37.650 --> 00:08:39.120
Act like it, would you?

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:46.590
Yamashiro...

00:08:51.740 --> 00:08:54.180
Shigure, it's not like that.

00:08:54.180 --> 00:08:56.060
I'm happy.

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:05.580
From now on, my sister and 
I will always be together.

00:09:11.160 --> 00:09:13.420
Shigure, this is for you.

00:09:14.730 --> 00:09:15.750
What is it?

00:09:16.180 --> 00:09:19.700
Something that perhaps 
we battleships didn't need.

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:23.090
But it's important that 
you have it. Take it.

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:31.030
Yamashiro, if we don't hurry, 
we'll miss our train.

00:09:31.030 --> 00:09:33.080
You're right, Sister.

00:09:35.160 --> 00:09:36.080
Admiral.

00:09:36.270 --> 00:09:37.230
Admiral.

00:09:38.350 --> 00:09:39.420
Yes.

00:09:58.040 --> 00:10:02.500
Mogami, Shigure... 
I'll see you again someday.

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:37.400
<b><b>1st Striking Force 3rd Section
Sasebo Naval District Detachment</b></b>

00:10:45.720 --> 00:10:48.940
It sure is quiet, now.

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:30.290
Oh, I'm...

00:11:36.740 --> 00:11:39.430
I'm supposed to go see the old man.

00:11:40.190 --> 00:11:41.090
The old...

00:11:41.090 --> 00:11:42.640
Oh, in the arsenal.

00:11:43.140 --> 00:11:45.880
He gets mouthy if you're late.

00:11:46.990 --> 00:11:49.290
I'm gonna head out. See you later.

00:12:03.290 --> 00:12:04.490
Do I...

00:12:05.660 --> 00:12:09.120
Do I belong here?

00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:12.770
Excuse me.

00:12:15.160 --> 00:12:16.360
Hatsushimo?

00:12:18.110 --> 00:12:20.930
Destroyer Shigure, 
the admiral is calling you.

00:12:21.630 --> 00:12:22.930
The admiral?

00:12:23.320 --> 00:12:24.730
That's all.

00:12:24.730 --> 00:12:26.920
Oh, understood.

00:12:29.360 --> 00:12:30.400
W-Wait.

00:12:58.240 --> 00:13:00.470
Destroyer Shigure, 
requesting permission to enter.

00:13:00.890 --> 00:13:01.840
Come in.

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:09.230
I'm here.

00:13:09.570 --> 00:13:12.180
Thanks. Sit down.

00:13:12.900 --> 00:13:14.490
That's all right, I'll stand.

00:13:14.490 --> 00:13:16.650
It's fine. Sit.

00:13:21.060 --> 00:13:22.660
All right, then.

00:13:33.550 --> 00:13:34.370
Thank you.

00:13:38.640 --> 00:13:43.160
First, you did well in assisting 
with Operation Shou-gou.

00:13:43.160 --> 00:13:44.010
Thank you.

00:13:44.010 --> 00:13:45.720
No, it was nothing...

00:13:46.140 --> 00:13:47.780
As you know...

00:13:50.970 --> 00:13:55.210
Thanks to the efforts of fleets from every 
naval district we have, the operation...

00:13:55.780 --> 00:13:57.110
was a success.

00:13:57.110 --> 00:13:59.780
Oh, Shigure, if you'd like some tea.

00:14:05.250 --> 00:14:07.160
Sure, thank you.

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:18.790
The enemy Abyssal advance force was badly 
damaged at the decisive battle of Leyte.

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:24.660
This has significantly delayed
 the timetable of their invasion.

00:14:26.490 --> 00:14:27.630
However...

00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:33.270
Accomplishing this task inflicted 
heavy damage on all fleets,

00:14:33.270 --> 00:14:36.800
including ours.

00:14:38.730 --> 00:14:44.160
The battleships Fusou and Yamashiro, 
and their escorts in Destroyer Division 4...

00:14:44.160 --> 00:14:46.330
They just barely made it out,

00:14:46.330 --> 00:14:51.470
but they'll never fight as Fleet Girls again.

00:14:55.500 --> 00:14:59.540
1st Striking Force, 3rd Section 
has been destroyed in all but name,

00:15:00.020 --> 00:15:01.310
and will be dismantled.

00:15:08.930 --> 00:15:12.280
The enemy has lost the bulk 
of their invasion force,

00:15:12.280 --> 00:15:16.400
but both their mobile and submarine 
fleets are essentially unharmed.

00:15:16.400 --> 00:15:19.740
And with our fleets forced to 
retreat from the front lines,

00:15:19.740 --> 00:15:23.610
our sea transport lines 
are exposed and defenseless.

00:15:27.870 --> 00:15:30.620
Shiratsuyu Class Destroyer, Shigure.

00:15:36.840 --> 00:15:39.380
Shiratsuyu Class Destroyer, Shigure!

00:15:40.600 --> 00:15:46.590
Destroyer Shigure, as of today, 
you are assigned to Torpedo Squadron 2.

00:15:47.290 --> 00:15:48.220
Yes, sir.

00:15:48.220 --> 00:15:51.680
I have received the order to be 
assigned to Torpedo Squadron 2.

00:15:54.470 --> 00:15:55.810
Torpedo Squadron 2...

00:15:57.560 --> 00:16:01.910
And Shigure, you're ordered
to half watch ashore.

00:16:03.020 --> 00:16:06.730
Things are bad, but rest comes first.

00:16:07.590 --> 00:16:09.670
This will be the only down time you get.

00:16:09.670 --> 00:16:10.910
Take it.

00:16:11.850 --> 00:16:13.200
Okay...

00:16:13.580 --> 00:16:17.250
Resting when you can is part of your job.

00:16:17.250 --> 00:16:19.370
I've got everything prepared.

00:16:28.410 --> 00:16:29.210
Yes, sir.

00:16:29.740 --> 00:16:31.920
I will now begin half watch ashore!

00:17:32.630 --> 00:17:36.570
<b>Saihi Motor Company</b>

00:17:36.570 --> 00:17:38.410
<b>Saihi Motor Company</b>

00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:44.960
Oh, um...

00:18:14.820 --> 00:18:17.280
<b>Women's Bath</b>

00:18:35.620 --> 00:18:37.720
Hey! We meet again!

00:18:42.270 --> 00:18:43.140
Yeah.

00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:45.950
I'm Yukikaze of Kure!

00:18:47.060 --> 00:18:48.190
I'm...

00:18:48.190 --> 00:18:49.480
I know you!

00:18:49.480 --> 00:18:50.950
You're Sasebo's...

00:18:51.640 --> 00:18:52.800
Shigure.

00:18:55.060 --> 00:18:57.960
I was born in Sasebo!

00:18:57.960 --> 00:19:00.390
Sasebo's a great place!

00:19:06.240 --> 00:19:08.830
It was so cool!

00:19:09.120 --> 00:19:11.420
I'm gonna <i>haunt</i> you!

00:19:56.520 --> 00:19:58.260
Thank you!

00:20:05.090 --> 00:20:05.930
<b>Saihi Motor Company</b>

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:11.920
All destroyers assigned to the new 
Torpedo Squadron 2 have arrived!

00:21:20.600 --> 00:21:23.090
Agano-Class Light Cruiser Yahagi.

00:21:23.560 --> 00:21:26.310
I will take command of Torpedo Squadron 2.

00:21:28.780 --> 00:21:32.440
As you know, things are nearing 
as bad as they can get.

00:21:34.630 --> 00:21:35.900
But remember...

00:21:36.640 --> 00:21:38.990
Torpedo Squadron 2 still stands!

00:21:39.700 --> 00:21:40.700
Let's do this!

00:23:29.050 --> 00:23:30.720
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:34.680 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Torpedo Squadron 2</b>

00:23:35.040 --> 00:23:39.390
Yukikaze of Kure, Shigure of Sasebo...
